            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous coronary artery dissection and pulmonary thromboembolism: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e21-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous coronary artery dissection (SCAD) still is a rare cause of acute coronary syndrome. SCAD has been observed in three groups of patients: those with coronary atherosclerosis, peripartal women and idiopathic group. SCAD may be associated with some conditions. We report an unusual association: SCAD and pulmonary thromboembolism.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
